## SQ-CDJ4-01 | CD mixins
@group A
@commands `grep -E "creativedelight.mixins.json\|Mixin apply.*creativedelight\|\[creativedelight\]" logs/latest.log`; `grep -c "from creativedelight.mixins.json" logs/debug.log`
@pass No mixin apply error; the 22 moved common mixins apply on a server (compartments `minecraft`, `quark`, `alexsmobs`, `immersive_weathering`, `farmersdelight`, `canned_goods`, `the_dirty_stuff`, `salt` with their mods loaded); none from `creativeengineering.mixins.json` for these names
@fails A compartment name is not the mod id, or Creative Common still lists a moved mixin
@from batches/r1101/cs4_boot3.qb
bootreject creativedelight\.mixins\.json.*(Error|error|failed)
shell grep -c "from creativedelight.mixins.json" logs/debug.log; grep -o "Mixing [A-Za-z_.]* from creativedelight.mixins.json" logs/debug.log | sed 's/Mixing //;s/ from.*//' | sort -u > cd_mx.txt; wc -l < cd_mx.txt; echo "also from CE:"; grep -o "Mixing [A-Za-z_.]* from creativeengineering.mixins.json" logs/debug.log | sed 's/Mixing //;s/ from.*//' | sort -u | comm -12 - cd_mx.txt; rm -f cd_mx.txt
look the moved common mixins apply from creativedelight.mixins.json, none also from creativeengineering.mixins.json

## SQ-CDJ4-02 | CD sections merged
@group A
@commands Same boot: `grep "\[swaps\] config sections" logs/latest.log`; read `config/creativedelight-common.toml`; restart, `grep "still has entries that moved" logs/latest.log`
@pass Merge line names the six sections and `perf`; CD file has `emptyCanChance = 0.5` and `[perf]` with only `troughMissCooldownTicks = 300`; CE file has none of them after the boot; second boot no WARN
@fails `mergeSections` ran after config load, or Forge kept the other `[perf]` keys
@from batches/r1101/cs4_boot3.qb
@superseded legacy config from 1.1.06, migration shipped in 1.2.00 and already ran on both machines (owner, 2026-11-18)
bootexpect \[swaps\] config sections .*canning.* merged from creativeengineering-common.toml into creativedelight-common.toml
shell grep -E "\[swaps\] config sections" logs/latest.log | cut -c60-300; grep -nE "^\s*\[|emptyCanChance|troughMissCooldownTicks" config/creativedelight-common.toml; echo "CD [perf] keys:"; awk '/^\[perf\]/{f=1;next} /^\[/{f=0} f && /=/' config/creativedelight-common.toml; echo CE:; grep -nE "^\[(crop_growth|dandelion_maturing|crop_drops|stem_fruit|canning|cooking)\]" config/creativeengineering-common.toml || echo "CE has none of the six"; grep -n "troughMissCooldownTicks" config/creativeengineering-common.toml || echo "CE has no troughMissCooldownTicks"
look merge names the six sections and perf; CD file emptyCanChance = 0.5, [perf] only troughMissCooldownTicks = 300; CE lost them

## SQ-CDJ4-03 | CD members, nested Baby Mobs and Incubation Additions
@group A
@commands Same boot: `grep "\[creativedelight\] members" logs/latest.log`; `grep -E "babymobs\|incubation_additions" logs/latest.log \| head`
@pass Member list ends with `babymobs, incubation_additions`; no "is loaded from ... not from the Creative Delight jar" ERROR
@fails A standalone jar left in `mods/`, or the bundle missed a member
@from batches/r1101/cs4_boot3.qb passed
@superseded premise obsolete: Baby Mobs nests in Creative Worldgen and Incubation Additions folded into CD compartments (M8), so the CD member list no longer ends with them (r1118 R1, 2026-11-18)
bootexpect \[creativedelight\] members: .*babymobs, incubation_additions
bootreject is loaded from .* not from the Creative Delight jar
shell grep -E "\[creativedelight\] members" logs/latest.log | cut -c60-400; ls mods | grep -iE "babymobs|incubationAdditions" || echo "no standalone jars"

